## Common commands

Everything goes through the Makefile; `make` alone lists the targets. These
are the ones the agent uses; the Makefile holds the real per-side commands.

```bash
make install                 # dependencies
make dev                     # dev server(s)
make lint                    # lint every side
make typecheck               # what CI type-checks
make test                    # all tests
make test-file FILE=<path>   # one test file (path relative to the side's folder)
<!-- {{IF FULLSTACK}} -->
make test-file-frontend FILE=<path>   # same, frontend side
<!-- {{ENDIF}} -->
make build                   # build every side
make up / make down          # local Docker stack (docker-compose.yml)
make logs                    # tail the stack
<!-- {{IF BACKEND}} -->
make up-backend              # rebuild + restart the backend container, tail its logs
<!-- {{ENDIF}} -->
<!-- {{IF FRONTEND}} -->
make up-frontend             # same for the frontend
<!-- {{ENDIF}} -->
<!-- {{IF BACKEND_PYTHON}} -->
make migrate                 # apply database migrations locally
<!-- {{ENDIF}} -->
```

Do not add a second way to run something that a make target already runs;
extend the Makefile instead.

