## Hard rules (do not violate)

<!-- {{IF BACKEND}} -->
- **Response envelope** on every JSON endpoint; paginated lists follow the
  standard in `.agents/rules/api-design.md`.
- **Errors are classes** from the shared hierarchy; never a raw status in a
  handler.
- **Every endpoint is guarded** on the route.
<!-- {{ENDIF}} -->
- **No new dependency, abstraction or pattern** without explicit approval.
- **No unrequested initiative**: only what was asked; report the rest.
- **Honest status**: a test is passed only if it ran in this session.
<!-- TODO(project): the project's own, e.g. "When adding or changing an index, bump `CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION`." -->

## Workflow for every task

1. Read this file and the `.agents/` documents listed above for the task.
2. Open the canonical reference for the layer you touch; mirror it.
3. Plan the smallest change; for anything beyond a local fix, follow
   `.agents/workflow/planning.md` and get confirmation.
4. Implement minimally (`.agents/workflow/implementation.md`).
5. Verify (`.agents/workflow/verification.md`): touched-area tests + build,
   real entry point, state what ran.
6. Hand off (`.agents/workflow/handoff.md`), then stop.

If you cannot satisfy a rule, **stop and ask** instead of bypassing it.

