## When in doubt

Prefer re-reading the `.agents/` documents and the canonical references over
guessing. Consistency with existing patterns matters more than cleverness.
The reviewer expects code that looks written by the same hand as the rest of
the project.

## Out of scope (do NOT do)

- Do not refactor unrelated code "while you're there".
- Do not introduce new libraries, abstractions or design patterns without
  being asked.
- Do not rename, reorganise or "clean up" files outside the requested change.
- Do not add tests, stories or documentation that were not requested beyond
  the definition of done.
- Do not change tooling configuration unless the task is about that
  configuration.
- Do not touch the git remote or any environment beyond the one the task
  names (`.agents/workflow/safety.md`).
